= Game theory — Technical =

A finite normal-form game is commonly written <pre>G = (N, (S_i), (u_i))</pre>with players N, strategy sets S_i, and payoff functions u_i. A profile s* is a Nash equilibrium if <pre>u_i(s_i*,s_-i*) ≥ u_i(s_i,s_-i*)</pre>for every player i and unilateral alternative s_i.

== Modeling cautions ==
* game theory ≠ zero-sum games only
* equilibrium ≠ social optimum
* game-theoretic model ≠ prediction without behavioral/institutional assumptions

